# HTTP Clients (Spring Boot)

## RestClient

- RestClient.create() or builder; get/post/put/delete; uri(), header(), body(); retrieve() or exchange(); type with ParameterizedTypeReference for generics.
- Set base URL from config; timeout (ClientHttpRequestFactory); interceptors for auth (Bearer), correlation ID header, logging.
- Error handling: onStatus to map 4xx/5xx to exception or Result; use DefaultResponseErrorHandler or custom.

## Declarative (HttpInterface)

- @HttpExchange on interface; @GetExchange, @PostExchange with path; @RequestHeader, @RequestBody, @PathVariable, @RequestParam.
- Return type: DTO, Mono/Flux (WebClient), or HttpEntity; register interface as bean with HttpServiceProxyFactory.
- Use for typed, centralized API contracts.

## Conventions

- Base URL and timeouts from config; retry/circuit breaker via Resilience4j; correlation ID in header; type-safe responses; do not log full body.

## Anti-Patterns

- No timeout; no retry for transients; hardcoded URL; logging request/response body with secrets

**See also:** `resilience.mdc`, `aggregation.mdc`
